      {
        "file": "CLAUDE.md",
        "comment": "html",
        "content": "## Prototype viewer (`explorations/present/`)\n\nPrototypes are explorations with a `prototype.json` (title, description, device, screens); the viewer shows them all to clients at `sites.metalab.com/<project>/present/`. Load the `prototype-viewer` skill before making a prototype or changing what a client sees.\n\n- `pnpm new-prototype <name>` — a new prototype, one screen per `#id` in `prototype.json`.\n- `pnpm present` — build every prototype and the viewer, and show them at http://localhost:4400.\n- A new prototype starts hidden from the client. Staff switch it on in the viewer's Prototypes panel, or Claude does through the Sites connection (the `present` site's `choices` collection).\n- `explorations/present/marcus/` is Marcus Brown's template, kept unchanged; viewer changes go in `explorations/present/live/`."
      }
    ]
  }
